-- ============================================================================
-- FC1 PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Separation & Slug Catching, intermediate tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: THE HORIZONTAL VESSEL AND THE PLOT. A circle cut by a
-- level, and the areas, the gas height and the chord that follow; the two
-- length requirements, the one that controls and the slenderness that falls
-- out; gas capacity in the gas space, its margin and its verdict; slug
-- catchers as a vessel and as a harp of fingers, sized from a working volume
-- that is larger than the slug; and distances on a site, where a table figure
-- is a table somebody copied and a flare or pool fire setback is computed
-- from its own duty.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. Gas can only control a horizontal vessel
-- that is already failing. The gas length is the velocity ratio times the gas
-- height and the capacity rule caps that ratio at 1, so every published case
-- where gas controls is a case where gasCapacityOk is false. A reader who
-- expects the gas length to be the binding one on a healthy vessel has the
-- verdict backwards.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. Half full is an assumption, not a property.
-- ABANA-2 at 8.000000 ft needs 23.270539 ft of length at a level of 0.500000
-- and 46.113917 ft at 0.300000, the same duty in a vessel twice as long,
-- because the level is an input a dump valve can move.
--
-- WHAT THE PROFESSIONAL AUDIT CAUGHT, and it is the shape of this tier's
-- hazard. An exam stem called the heater treater's 9.3696 m the smallest
-- shortfall on the plot. The plot's smallest is 1.7933 m, the pump pair the
-- course teaches everywhere else as the small breach a reader scanning for
-- large numbers walks past. 9.3696 m is the smallest of the four RADIATION
-- breaches, and the stem now says so.
--
-- The only numbers that travel from this tier to the next are the
-- cross-section geometry, the two length requirements and the layout check's
-- four answers.
-- ============================================================================

